Known failure: range-stable — range-formatting one line of a multi-line statement adds ';' and re-indents a continuation line (#325)
Expression continuations that begin with a binary operator (`+`, `.AND.`,
`$`) take one level of continuation indent past the statement line
(fmt.indent_style, issue #86); input lines are flush-left or over-indented.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Describe;
:PARAMETERS sName, sStatus, nCount;
:DECLARE sOut, bShow;
sOut := "Sample " + sName
+ " is " + sStatus
                + " with " + LimsString(nCount) + " results";
bShow := nCount > 0
.AND. "X" $ sStatus
.OR. Empty(sName);
:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Describe;
	:PARAMETERS sName, sStatus, nCount;
	:DECLARE sOut, bShow;
	sOut := "Sample " + sName
		+ " is " + sStatus
		+ " with " + LimsString(nCount) + " results";
	bShow := nCount > 0
		.AND. "X" $ sStatus
		.OR. Empty(sName);
	:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
